WEBVTT

scene-1
00:00:00.194 --> 00:00:04.692
1. Overview: six machines live at 60× (plant 06:01–06:05)
The operator sees the six machines live; the plant clock follows the run at 60×.

scene-2
00:00:04.697 --> 00:00:10.519
2. Orders: release and dispatch; the CNCs accept (plant 06:05–06:11)
The supervisor releases and dispatches the four ERP orders; each CNC accepts its job (OPC UA LoadOrder).

scene-3
00:00:10.522 --> 00:00:19.359
3. Console: status, timeline progress, pause and resume (plant 06:11–06:17)
The admin sees the run paused by the timeline at 06:14, its progress list; resume, pause, resume.

wait-4
00:00:19.359 --> 00:01:22.459
The run goes on at 60× (plant 06:17 to 07:20); scene 4 opens at 07:20.

scene-4
00:01:22.459 --> 00:01:55.742
4. Alarms and downtime: acknowledged, breakdown coded (plant 07:20–07:53)
Maintenance acknowledges the spindle overload on CNC-01; after the repair, codes its breakdown.

wait-5
00:01:55.742 --> 00:03:02.443
The run goes on at 60× (plant 07:53 to 09:00); scene 5 opens at 09:00.

scene-5
00:03:02.443 --> 00:03:07.455
5. OEE: availability loss, bottleneck, an order’s OEE (plant 09:00–09:05)
The supervisor sees CNC-01’s availability loss, the line’s bottleneck (ASM-01), an order’s OEE and first-pass yield.

wait-6
00:03:07.455 --> 00:06:02.352
The run goes on at 60× (plant 09:05 to 12:00); scene 6 opens at 12:00.

scene-6
00:06:02.352 --> 00:06:05.883
6. SPC: the leak test’s drift episode (plant 12:00–12:03)
The quality user sees the leak test’s SPC chart with the drift’s first episode.

scene-7
00:06:05.889 --> 00:06:31.060
7. Hold: from the episode; the close refused (plant 12:03–12:28)
A hold from the episode, its scope on the holds screen; the order’s close refused while held.

scene-8
00:06:31.062 --> 00:06:34.742
8. Traceability: a packed serial back, its blank lot forward (plant 12:28–12:32)
A packed serial traced back to its lots, machines, operator and leak value; its blank lot forward to its cartons.
